rms of Ernest August, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg (1661-1692).svg","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Electorate_of_Mainz.svg"}},"grand-duchy-of-berg":{"img":"/images/states/grand-duchy-of-berg.jpg","cr":{"a":"Sir Iain","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Grand_Duchy_of_Berg_(1806-1808).svg"}},"german-east-africa":{"img":"/images/states/german-east-africa.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Imperial Colonial Office of the German Empire Vector: David Liuzzo","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichskolonialflagge.svg"}},"governorate-of-new-castile":{"img":"/images/states/governorate-of-new-castile.jpg","cr":{"a":"Ningyou.","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cross_of_Burgundy.svg"}},"geshur":{"img":"/images/states/geshur.jpg","cr":{"a":"AnonMoos","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Early-Historical-Israel-Dan-Beersheba-Judea.png"}},"german-new-guinea":{"img":"/images/states/german-new-guinea.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Imperial Colonial Office of the German Empire Vector: David Liuzzo","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichskolonialflagge.svg"}},"german-samoa":{"img":"/images/states/german-samoa.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Imperial Colonial Office of the German Empire Vector: David Liuzzo","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichskolonialflagge.svg"}},"gangani-britain":{"t":"People of the Llŷn peninsula in north-west Wales, known from a headland Ptolemy named after them, with namesakes in western Ireland.","o":"Ptolemy\u0027s Geography of about 150 names a Ganganorum Promontorium, the headland of the Gangani, on the coast of north-west Wales, generally identified with the tip of the Llŷn peninsula. Ptolemy does not list the Gangani among the inland peoples, so they may have been a small coastal group or a subdivision of the Ordovices.","r":"Nothing is known of their rulers or society. Llŷn was a land of hillforts such as Tre\u0027r Ceiri, a stone-walled settlement occupied into the Roman period, and of farming and fishing communities. The identical name in Ireland, borne by the Gangani (Ireland) on the Shannon, has prompted theories of migration across the Irish Sea in either direction.","e":"The Gangani are not mentioned again. Llŷn later saw Irish settlement in the post-Roman period and became part of the Kingdom of Gwynedd.","re":"Celtic polytheism","la":"Common Brittonic","c":"low"},"gaoche":{"img":"/images/states/gaoche.jpg","cr":{"a":"Author: Benjamin Banayan (rugrabbit.com), photographed at the Metropolitan Museum of Art exhibit \"COURT AND COSMOS: T...","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Court_of_Seljuk_ruler_Tughril_III.jpg"}},"golden-horde":{"img":"/images/states/golden-horde.jpg","cr":{"a":"naturalearthdata.com, offered to the Public Domain per Terms of Use","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Golden_Horde_(with_text).png"}},"grand-duchy-of-luxembourg":{"img":"/images/states/grand-duchy-of-luxembourg.jpg","cr":{"a":"Drawn by User:SKopp","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Luxembourg.svg"}},"giri-kedaton":{"img":"/images/states/giri-kedaton.jpg","cr":{"a":"H. A. Buchory Rachman","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giri_Kedaton-Gapura.jpg"}},"gilbert-and-ellice-islands":{"img":"/images/states/gilbert-and-ellice-islands.jpg","cr":{"a":"Telim tor (original) Orange Tuesday (most recent)","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Gilbert_and_Ellice_Islands_(1937%E2%80%931976).svg"}},"goryeong-gaya":{"img":"/images/states/goryeong-gaya.jpg","cr":{"a":"Asieon","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5th_century_Kaya_confederacy.png"}},"goguryeo":{"img":"/images/states/goguryeo.jpg","cr":{"a":"Asieon","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5th_century_Goguryeo.png"}},"guler-state":{"img":"/images/states/guler-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Surveyed by Alexander Cunningham, drawn by Kalleemoodden","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detail_of_the_main,_continuous_tract_of_territory_of_Guler_from_a_map_of_the_various_Hill_States_of_the_Punjab_Hills_region,_copied_in_1852.jpg"}},"gallic-empire":{"img":"/images/states/gallic-empire.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original - ArdadN ; edit - Wario2.","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GallicEmpire262.png"}},"gongsun-yan":{"img":"/images/states/gongsun-yan.jpg","cr":{"a":"Three Kingdoms fan","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Three_Kingdoms_timelapse.gif"}},"grand-principality-of-transylvania":{"img":"/images/states/grand-principality-of-transylvania.jpg","cr":{"a":"J Darnley at English Wikipedia","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Transylvania_before_1918.svg"}},"gela":{"t":"Rhodian and Cretan colony on Sicily\u0027s south coast whose tyrants, Hippocrates and Gelon, built the first great Greek power on the island.","o":"Colonists from Lindos on Rhodes and from Crete, led by Antiphemus and Entimus, founded Gela around 689 BCE on a long ridge by the Gela river, inland of a sandy coast. The colony pushed into the Sicel interior and in 580 BCE founded Acragas to the west.","r":"Gela reached its peak under the tyrants Cleander and Hippocrates, who around 495 BCE dominated much of eastern Sicily, and under Gelon, who seized Syracuse in 485 BCE and moved half of Gela\u0027s people there. Its farmland produced grain and horses, and its terracotta workshops and coins with a man-headed bull were renowned. The playwright Aeschylus died there in 456 BCE.","e":"Carthage sacked Gela in 405 BCE. Timoleon resettled it in the 330s BCE, but in 282 BCE Phintias, tyrant of Acragas, destroyed it and moved its people to his new city at Licata. The site was refounded by Frederick II in 1233 as Terranova, renamed Gela in 1927.","ru":["Hippocrates","Gelon"],"re":"Greek religion","la":"Doric Greek","img":"/images/states/gela.jpg","cr":{"a":"AbelDionis","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gela_Panorama.png"}},"gangga-negara":{"img":"/images/states/gangga-negara.jpg","cr":{"a":"Lilauid (talk · contribs)","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_Malaya_circa_1922_en.svg"}},"government-of-national-salvation":{"img":"/images/states/government-of-national-salvation.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original author: Government of National Salvation (Nedics Serbia), Redraw: Samhanin (SVG file author), WikiNameBaks (...","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Government_of_National_Salvation_2.svg"}},"goryeo":{"img":"/images/states/goryeo.jpg","cr":{"a":"Historyclassproffesor","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Koryo_map.png"}},"gujarat-sultanate":{"img":"/images/states/gujarat-sultanate.jpg","cr":{"a":"Beylarbey","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Political_boundary_of_the_Gujarat_Sultanate_in_1490.png"}},"greco-bactrian-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/greco-bactrian-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"No machine-readable author provided. World Imaging assumed (based on copyright claims).","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greco-BactrianKingdomMap.jpg"}},"grand-duchy-of-baden":{"img":"/images/states/grand-duchy-of-baden.jpg","cr":{"a":"David Liuzzo","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Gro%C3%9Fherzogtum_Baden_(1891%E2%80%931918).svg"}},"garhwal-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/garhwal-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"Robert Alfers","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Princely_State_of_Tehri_Garhwal.svg"}},"governorate-of-livonia":{"img":"/images/states/governorate-of-livonia.jpg","cr":{"a":"Milenioscuro","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0"