las_en_Am%C3%A9rica_del_Sur_(1534-1539).svg"}},"greuthungi":{"img":"/images/states/greuthungi.jpg","cr":{"a":"en:User:Wiglaf, en:User:Dbachmann","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chernyakhov.PNG"}},"griqualand-east":{"img":"/images/states/griqualand-east.jpg","cr":{"a":"Seb az86556","l":"CC BY 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FlagGriekwalandEast.svg"}},"gangpur-state":{"img":"/images/states/gangpur-state.jpg","cr":{"a":"Great Britain India Office","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orissa_Tributary_States-IGI.jpg"}},"gombe-emirate":{"img":"/images/states/gombe-emirate.jpg","cr":{"a":"United States Depart of State, US Embassy to Nigeria","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emir_of_Gombe_Gribbin_2007.jpg"}},"great-sioux-nation":{"img":"/images/states/great-sioux-nation.jpg","cr":{"a":"David F. Barry, Photographer, Bismarck, Dakota Territory","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sitting_Bull_by_D_F_Barry_ca_1883_Dakota_Territory.jpg"}},"germiyanids":{"img":"/images/states/germiyanids.jpg","cr":{"a":"Gabagool","l":"CC BY 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatolia1300.png"}},"goree":{"img":"/images/states/goree.jpg","cr":{"a":"Gregor Rom","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ile-de-goree.jpg"}},"galatia":{"img":"/images/states/galatia.jpg","cr":{"a":"SilverStar54","l":"CC BY 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galatia.svg"}},"gaza-empire":{"img":"/images/states/gaza-empire.jpg","cr":{"a":"Ypirétis","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carte_royaume_de_gaza.gif"}},"gadir":{"t":"The great Phoenician city of Cádiz, gateway to the Atlantic, home of a famous temple of Melqart and one of the oldest continuously inhabited cities in Europe.","o":"Gadir was founded by settlers from Tyre on islands off the Atlantic coast near the mouth of the Guadalete. Ancient writers dated its foundation to around 1100 BCE, but archaeology places it in the 9th to 8th centuries BCE. Its position beyond the Strait of Gibraltar gave access to Tartessian silver and Atlantic tin.","r":"Gadir was governed by its own elite under institutions modelled on Tyre, and its temple of Melqart, later identified with Hercules, drew pilgrims from across the Mediterranean; Hannibal visited before marching on Italy in 218 BCE. Fish salting, purple dye and long-distance trade made it rich, and it came to lead the Phoenician towns of the south under Carthaginian hegemony.","e":"In 206 BCE, after the Carthaginian defeat at Ilipa, Gadir went over to Rome under a treaty of alliance. Its citizens received Roman citizenship under Julius Caesar, and Gades became one of the wealthiest cities of Hispania Baetica.","re":"Phoenician religion","la":"Phoenician","c":"medium"},"governorate-of-buenos-aires":{"img":"/images/states/governorate-of-buenos-aires.jpg","cr":{"a":"Raul Senzacqua","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casa_y_monta%C3%B1a.jpg"}},"greater-lebanon":{"img":"/images/states/greater-lebanon.jpg","cr":{"a":"Ch1902","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lebanon_during_French_Mandate_(1920-1943).svg"}},"ganzhou-uyghur-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/ganzhou-uyghur-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"SY","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guiyi_Circuit.png"}},"governorate-of-new-toledo":{"img":"/images/states/governorate-of-new-toledo.jpg","cr":{"a":"Ningyou.","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cross_of_Burgundy.svg"}},"grand-principality-of-serbia":{"img":"/images/states/grand-principality-of-serbia.jpg","cr":{"a":"Boban Markovic","l":"CC BY-SA 2.5","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Serbie_de_Nemanja_1184.svg"}},"grenada":{"img":"/images/states/grenada.jpg","cr":{"a":"See file history below for details.","l":"Public domain","s":"https://c